     "text": "{\n  \"steps\": [\n    \"Check ST30-WLD tag air_pressure_bar leading up to 2026-08-07T14:35:15Z; values dropping below 5.3 bar support a verified low pressure condition at the weld gun, whereas readings remaining within 5.3 to 5.9 bar refute an actual pressure drop and suggest false alarming.\",\n    \"Check UT-AIR tags header_pressure_bar, compressor_current_a, and oil_temp_c prior to the stop event; header pressure below 6.0 bar or abnormal compressor current supports a plant-wide or utility compressed air supply failure, whereas normal header pressure (6.0 to 7.5 bar) refutes utility failure and isolates the drop to ST30's branch.\",\n    \"Check upstream ST20-WLD tag air_pressure_bar over the same time window; a concurrent pressure drop below 5.3 bar supports a common header or shared branch feed line issue affecting welding cells, while normal pressure (5.3 to 5.9 bar) refutes a common feed issue and points to a local ST30 pneumatic leak or valve failure.\",\n    \"Inspect ST30-WLD air_pressure_bar signal characteristics for sudden drop to null/zero, flatline, or erratic high-frequency noise without physical air consumption correlation to test if this is a pressure transmitter or wiring fault rather than a physical pneumatic drop.\",\n    \"Check ST30-WLD tags cycle_time_s, tip_resistance_mohm, and servo_temp_c leading into the stop; abnormal cycle times (>55 s) or elevated servo temperature (>65 degC) support mechanical binding or actuator overload depleting air, while normal values refute upstream weld cycle distress.\",\n    \"Review maintenance logs and recent work orders for ST30-WLD and UT-AIR for recent pneumatic fitting, regulator adjustment, or sensor calibration; recent pneumatic servicing supports maintenance-induced leakage or incorrect regulator setpoint, while absence refutes recent human error.\"\n  ],\n  \"upstream_step\": 1,\n  \"sensor_step\": 3,\n  \"suspects\": [\n    \"ST30-WLD\",\n    \"UT-AIR\",\n    \"ST20-WLD\"\n  ]\n} "
